  "prefLabel": "Env-A 1203.62 Over-varnish",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-A 1203.62 \"Over-varnish\" means a coating applied directly over a design coating or directly over ink to reduce the coefficient of friction, to provide gloss, and to protect the finish against abrasion and corrosion.\n\nSource. (See Revision Note at chapter heading for Env-A 1200) #9933, eff 6-1-11; ss by #12899, eff 10-17-19",
